WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.110
What is the dumbest

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.100
and most physically dangerous
thing you've ever done?

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.400
Okay, I know exactly what it is.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.720
There's actually, there's a couple because

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.460
I mean, there's more than one.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.210
When I get thinking
about what might be funny

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.180
or in front of people,

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.430
my good sense tends to go away.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:23.960
So on tour in I think 2010,

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:28.010
we did this very raucous show

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.060
that we toured around the country

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.350
and it was in large venues

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.480
and I would do all kinds of comedy,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.384
but I would also play the
guitar and do musical numbers.

00:00:39.384 --> 00:00:41.510
And it just started to,

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:43.450
the crowds were getting bigger and bigger

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.710
and it was turning into,

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.470
it was so chaotic

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.270
and there was so much energy,

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.480
that I remembered one time I ran up,

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.680
I had pretty much a
radio mic on my guitar,

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.150
so I could go anywhere with the guitar

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.100
and I ran up with my guitar
to the second balcony

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.531
and I stood on the edge of
the balcony playing the guitar

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:07.405
and didn't even think about it.

00:01:07.405 --> 00:01:12.405
And the people who I employ
were furious with me.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.060
They were watching it and
they were like, you asshole,

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.490
you were standing there not even looking

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:22.400
at what you were doing and you
so easily could have fallen

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.670
and it was, you know, a 30 foot fall.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:27.310
It wouldn't have gone well.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.070
That was super stupid

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:32.030
and I was very apologetic and,

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:34.920
but I was living out some weird,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.240
hey, look at me, I'm Eddie
Van Halen guitar fantasy

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.500
and it was just stupid.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.060
The second one, we were
doing a rehearsal once

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:49.480
with animals and there was
a very large water buffalo

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.130
I think from Africa

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.930
and someone just said,

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:55.390
hey it might be funny if you got on it.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:58.790
And the trainer who
actually knew nothing about,

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:00.260
who was just there to hold the animals

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.480
and didn't know that much
about each particular one

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.267
she said, yeah, get on it.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.940
And I said, okay.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.360
And I later looked back at
the footage 'cause we were

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.230
shooting it for rehearsal

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.010
and I just said, you probably
remember this too, Sona.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.860
And so I went, yeah okay

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.980
and I jumped on the
back of a water buffalo.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:17.904
Now let me be clear,

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.130
a water buffalo, this water buffalo

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:24.350
was the size of a mid-size compact car.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.450
And I jumped on the back of it

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:29.470
and this water buffalo
didn't want me on its back.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:31.640
So the first thing it did
Wonder why.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.540
was threw me off and I landed

00:02:35.446 --> 00:02:40.030
on a solid concrete
floor that's extra dense

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:42.020
so that you can roll TV cameras on it

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:45.100
and I bounced off my left hip

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.600
and the buffalo charged forward,

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.100
knocked a bunch of cameras over,

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.640
then turned around and I,

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.530
all I saw was the whites of its eyes

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.610
and started charging at me.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:59.690
And I ran like a cartoon character

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.370
and like made a hole in the wall

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.053
that was in the shape of my body.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.290
I got a massive hematoma,

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.853
it was so big, I couldn't
get my pants off.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:12.390
And I was like,

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.340
thinking back to it when
we looked at the tape,

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.460
my sidekick, Andy Richter's standing there

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.560
and, or sitting there

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.550
and he's not really paying attention

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.800
and in fact nobody's paying attention.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.730
But what you can hear is someone says,

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.750
I think a segment producer
says, why don't you get on?

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:28.680
What if you got on it?

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.030
And then the trainer
goes, yeah, get on it.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.160
I say, yeah, I'll get on it.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:37.286
And then you hear Andy Richter
say, I wouldn't do that.

00:03:37.286 --> 00:03:38.370
(laughing)

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:39.740
And he says it at about that level.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.884
He goes and he, I think he's like

00:03:41.884 --> 00:03:43.810
playing with his phone at the same time.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:45.520
He goes, I wouldn't do that.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.353
So just putting

00:03:46.353 --> 00:03:47.186
it on record.
Yeah.

00:03:47.186 --> 00:03:48.255
Not trying to really stop you.
He just, he wasn't,

00:03:48.255 --> 00:03:49.585
yeah, exactly.

00:03:49.585 --> 00:03:52.430
Just, he just says,
eh, I wouldn't do that.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:53.665
And then you just see me--

00:03:53.665 --> 00:03:54.600
He still wanted to see what would happen.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.750
Yeah and then I instantly jump on the,

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:57.720
I don't listen to him.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.360
I jump on the back of the water buffalo

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.020
and it's all like my sympathy

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.670
is... the water buffalo is right.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:05.660
It was in the right,

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.070
I was in the wrong.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:09.960
And so, yeah and I think if

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:13.170
I thought about it I can
think of 600 more of those.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.066
I just

00:04:14.066 --> 00:04:15.626
(laughing)

00:04:15.626 --> 00:04:18.830
and I have nobody to blame, but myself,

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:22.434
but I never said I was the smartest guy.

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:24.653
I'm just--
Never thought it.

00:04:24.653 --> 00:04:25.486
Yeah,

00:04:25.486 --> 00:04:26.319
oh okay.

00:04:26.319 --> 00:04:27.152
All right.

00:04:27.152 --> 00:04:27.985
(laughing)

00:04:27.985 --> 00:04:28.818
All right.

00:04:28.818 --> 00:04:31.510
All right, Lux.
Lux et veritas.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:32.800
Lux,

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.250
Lux I'm gonna come to London.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.430
I get there sometimes and
I'm gonna find you, man.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:38.340
Okay.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.324
And we're gonna settle
this once and for all.

00:04:40.324 --> 00:04:41.250
Oh yeah, all right.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:42.490
Which means that you're going to

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.315
with your upper body strength

00:04:44.315 --> 00:04:46.971
instantly beat the crap out of me.

00:04:46.971 --> 00:04:49.040
To be fair, Conan, I'm quite a short guy.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:49.873
So you could--

00:04:49.873 --> 00:04:51.090
I don't think I,

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.410
no, my height is of no advantage,

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:54.773
trust me, the way I use it.

